{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.csm.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Administrative-Assistant-Academic-Affairs-8-2026-DRAFT.pdf": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, Academic Affairs",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant, Academic Affairs.  \n \nCollege of Saint Mary is a Catholic university providing access to education for women in an environment that calls \nforth potential and fosters leadership. The University is an equal employment opportunity employer and does not \ndiscriminate against employees or job applicants on the basis of race, religion, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender \nidentity, pregnancy, age, national origin, disability, veteran status, marital status or any other status or condition \nprotected by applicable laws, except where a bona fide occupational qualification applies.  \n \n \nAdministrative Assistant, Academic Affairs \n \nJoin Our Academic Affairs Team at College of Saint Mary \nCollege of Saint Mary is focused first on students and their excellence, and seeks an Administrative \nAssistant to support senior leaders and help keep academic affairs running smoothly. This role sits at the \nintersection of organization, communication, and mission – and it matters. \n \nAre You Someone Who: \n• Takes initiative and uses sound judgment to solve problems and keep things moving  \n• Communicates well and builds strong working relationships across campus \n• Stays organized while juggling multiple priorities and deadlines \n• Enjoys supporting meaningful work in a collaborative environment \n \nDoes Your Education and Experience Include: \n• A bachelor’s degree \n• At least three years of executive administrative assistant experience in higher education or a related field  \n \nWhat You’ll Do: \nAdministrative Support \n• Provide direct administrative support to the VPAA and Assistant Deans \n• Serve as recording secretary for institutional and division committees \n• Support daily administrative functions and key academic affairs initiatives \nOperations and Coordination \n• Reconcile monthly expenditures and support financial tracking \n• Manage personnel files, contracts, onboarding, and monthly payroll reports for adjunct and \noverload requests in collaboration with Human Resources \n• Maintain institutional data in the CSM Data Repository \n• Manage division communications and support event planning for graduation and honors  \nStudent and Faculty Support \n• Serve as a liaison for faculty, staff, and students in the Office of Academic Affairs \n• Support the student academic decision process, including communication related to \nacademic awards, probation, dismissal, and appeals \n \nWhy CSM?  \n• Mission-driven work. You'll be part of a team united by a genuine commitment to serving \nstudents and the broader community.  \n• Great benefits. Full-time employees are eligible for health insurance, paid time off, tuition \nremission, a 403(b) with an employer match, employee wellness time, and more! \n \nApplication: \nPlease have a resume, cover letter, and contact information for three professional references, including \none supervisor, ready to upload during the application process. \n \nPlease apply using the following link:   Administrative Assistant, Academic Affairs "
    },
    "https://www.csm.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/IT-Help-Desk-Support-Specialist-9-2026.pdf": {
      "title": "IT Help Desk Support Specialist",
      "description": "IT Help Desk Support Specialist.  \n \nCollege of Saint Mary is a Catholic university providing access to education for women in an environment that calls \nforth potential and fosters leadership. The University is an equal employment opportunity employer and does not \ndiscriminate against employees or job applicants on the basis of race, religion, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender \nidentity, pregnancy, age, national origin, disability, veteran status, marital status or any other status or condition \nprotected by applicable laws, except where a bona fide occupational qualification applies.  \n \n \nIT Help Desk Support Specialist \n \nJoin Our Information Technology Team at College of Saint Mary \nAt College of Saint Mary, student success is at the heart of everything we do, and we seek an IT Help Desk \nSupport Specialist to provide responsive, reliable technology support for faculty, staff, and students.  \n \nAre You Someone Who: \n• Enjoys helping people and providing excellent end-user support \n• Takes an inquisitive, resourceful approach to solving technical problems \n• Communicates clearly with both technical and non-technical audiences \n• Stays organized while managing multiple requests and priorities \n• Works well in a collaborative, service-driven environment \n \nDoes Your Education and Experience Include: \n• An associate’s degree in computer science  \n• At least two years of help desk support experience \n• Strong knowledge of Windows 10 and Windows 11 \n• Help desk ticketing system experience preferred \n \nWhat You’ll Do \nTechnical Support \n• Provide general technical support for College of Saint Mary faculty, staff, and students \n• Respond to day-to-day questions and document interactions in the help desk system \n• Research and communicate technical malfunctions as they arise \nCampus Technology Support \n• Install and maintain various technology setups and equipment across campus \n• Provide audio/visual support to the campus community \n• Work with vendors to repair or replace equipment, and perform repairs on campus \ntechnology when needed \nDocumentation and Communication \n• Create and update knowledge base documentation \n• Help ensure support information is accurate, accessible, and useful for the campus community \n \nWhy CSM? \n• Mission-driven work. You’ll be part of a team united by a genuine commitment to serving \nstudents and the broader community. \n• Great benefits. Full-time employees are eligible for health insurance, paid time off, tuition \nremission, a 403(b) with employer match, employee wellness time, and more. \n \nApplication \nPlease have a resume, cover letter, and contact information for three professional references, including \none supervisor, ready to upload during the application process. \n \nPlease apply using the following link: IT Help Desk Support Specialist "
    },
    "https://www.csm.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Safety-and-Security-Officer-PT-10-2026.pdf": {
      "title": "Safety and Security Officer",
      "description": "Safety and Security Officer.  \n \nCollege of Saint Mary is a Catholic university providing access to education for women in an environment that calls \nforth potential and fosters leadership. The University is an equal employment opportunity employer and does not \ndiscriminate against employees or job applicants on the basis of race, religion, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender \nidentity, pregnancy, age, national origin, disability, veteran status, marital status or any other status or condition \nprotected by applicable laws, except where a bona fide occupational qualification applies.  \n \n \n \nSafety & Security Officer \n(Part-time) \n \nCSM is seeking a security professional to join the Safety and Security Department. This position \nserves on mutually agreed-upon shifts and reports to the Director of Safety and Security. \n \nOur Ideal Candidate’s Preferred Education and Experience Include: \n• High school degree or equivalent is required.  \n• Law enforcement, security or military experience is preferred.  \n• Possess a valid driver’s license. \n• Ability to complete and maintain CPR certification within 90 days of hire. \n \nThis Position: \n• Conduct vehicle and foot patrols.        \n• Perform physical security checks of campus facilities. \n• Observes, reports, and identifies persons involved in suspicious activities, including suspicious \nvehicles, and ensures unauthorized persons leave College of Saint Mary property.  \n• Enforces college policies, regulations, and municipal, state, and federal laws, assisting local law \nenforcement when requested or necessary. \n• Responds to emergency calls for assistance including medical matters, fire alarms and other \nalarms including those relating to facility operations such as boiler system, etc.  \n• Locks and unlocks campus buildings, classrooms, and offices as necessary. \n• Response to routine calls for assistance including safety walks and vehicle jumpstarts.  \n \nWhy You Want to Be on This Team: \n• You would be a part of a mission-centered team, who work together to serve our community. \n• Regular professional development opportunities available for the safety and security team. \n• CSM is committed to supporting the work-life balance of its faculty and staff. \n \nApplication \nPlease have a resume, cover letter, and contact information for three professional references, including \none supervisor, ready to upload during the application process. \n \nPlease apply using the following link: Safety and Security Officer \n \n "
    },
    "https://www.csm.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/DPT-Faculty-9-2026.pdf": {
      "title": "DPT Faculty",
      "description": "DPT Faculty.  \n \nCollege of Saint Mary is a Catholic university providing access to education for women in an environment that calls \nforth potential and fosters leadership. The University is an equal employment opportunity employer and does not \ndiscriminate against employees or job applicants on the basis of race, religion, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender \nidentity, pregnancy, age, national origin, disability, veteran status, marital status or any other status or condition \nprotected by applicable laws, except where a bona fide occupational qualification applies.  \n \n \n \nDoctor of Physical Therapy Faculty \n \nThe College of Saint Mary (CSM) Division of Health Professions invites applications for a full-time, 12-\nmonth, non-tenured faculty appointment at the Assistant or Associate Professor rank for a hybrid Doctor of \nPhysical Therapy (DPT) program in Omaha, NE. The ideal candidate will have experience and expertise \nteaching cardiovascular and pulmonary, acute care, pharmacology, and pathophysiology. The DPT program \nis completed in 2.5 years and uses a combination of online and face-to-face learning experiences to \neducate future practitioners. The blended learning model allows faculty and students to live remotely from \ncampus. However, DPT faculty must travel to and stay in Omaha for designated periods each semester.  \n \nThe successful candidate's responsibilities include developing content and teaching courses that emphasize \nexamination and intervention for patients/clients with movement dysfunctions; other teaching \nresponsibilities will be considered. In addition, this faculty member will assist with mentoring in related \nareas of expertise within the CSM DPT Clinical Education Program and serve as a clinical instructor during \nintegrated clinical education experiences. The candidate will develop and sustain an independent research \nagenda. Other expectations include participating in curriculum development and student advising; \nproviding treatment and/or mentorship in pro bono clinics; completing clinical education site visits; \nassisting with student recruitment and retention efforts; participating in college and department \naccreditation activities; and providing service to the department, college, community, and the profession. \nProfessional service and active participation in the American Physical Therapy Association are imperative. \nThe successful candidate must work well in a team environment, build inclusive learning communities, and \nbe comfortable working independently. The ideal candidate will also have strong communication, problem-\nsolving, clinical reasoning, organizational, and self-assessment skills.  \n \nMinimum Qualifications Education & Experience Requirements:  \n• Graduate of an accredited physical therapist education program \n• A terminal physical therapy degree (DPT) or a physical therapy degree with an academic \nterminal degree (PhD, EdD, DHSc). All degrees must be earned from an accredited institution.  \n• Should be licensed or eligible for licensure in Nebraska \n• Member of the American Physical Therapy Association \n• Prior teaching experience in a physical therapist or physical therapist assistant education program \n• Board-certified clinical specialists or clinical physical therapy residency graduates (i.e., acute \ncare, cardiovascular and pulmonary) preferred  \n• Minimum of 5 years of experience as a licensed physical therapist \n• Able to work with students with special needs based on the Americans with Disabilities Act \n• Prior teaching experience in distance education preferred \n• Knowledge of educational management and adult learning theories and principles preferred \n \nApplication: \nPlease complete the application, send a cover letter, provide a current curriculum vitae and contact \ninformation for three professional references ready to upload during the application process. \n \nApply using the following link: Doctor of Physical Therapy Faculty "
    },
    "https://www.csm.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/PA-Faculty-6-2026.pdf": {
      "title": "Physician Assistant Studies Faculty",
      "description": "Physician Assistant Studies Faculty.  \n \nCollege of Saint Mary is a Catholic university providing access to education for women in an environment that calls \nforth potential and fosters leadership. The University is an equal employment opportunity employer and does not \ndiscriminate against employees or job applicants on the basis of race, religion, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender \nidentity, pregnancy, age, national origin, disability, veteran status, marital status or any other status or condition \nprotected by applicable laws, except where a bona fide occupational qualification applies.  \n \n \n \nPhysician Assistant Studies Faculty \n \nJoin Our PA Studies Program Team at College of Saint Mary \nAt College of Saint Mary, students come first — and everything we do flows from that commitment. We're \nlooking for a positive, energetic, and caring educator to join a close -knit faculty who genuinely love to \nteach. If you're passionate about developing the next generation of healthcare providers in a supportive, \nmission-driven environment, we'd like to meet you. \n \nThis is an open -rank, full-time percentage (0.8) faculty position teaching 18 credit hours per 12-month \nacademic year in a program that puts students at the center of everything. \n \nOur Ideal Candidate Is Someone Who: \n• Gets excited about working with students from all walks of life. \n• Stays curious — you're always learning and open to trying new approaches. \n• Thrives in a collaborative environment where the team's success matters as much as your own. \n \nOur Ideal Candidate’s Education and Experience: \n• Completion of an accredited Physician Assistant Program from an accredited college or \nuniversity, or allied health degree in a relevant field is preferred.  \n• Minimum of 2 years of clinical experience as a physician assistant or healthcare provider. \n• Master’s degree in appropriate field, doctoral degree preferred.  \n• Preferred qualification: experience with or interest in graduate remediation.  \n \nThis Position Is Responsible For: \n• Works collaboratively with PA Faculty who are responsible for developing and guiding the \ncurriculum for PA students.  \n• Teach 18 credit hours. \n• Participates in the program’s ongoing self-study, accreditation, and continuous improvement \nprocesses.  \n \nWhy CSM?  Here are a few more reasons to consider us: \n• Mission matters here. Our team is united by a shared commitment to serving our students and \nour broader community. \n• Great benefits. Full-time faculty enjoy health insurance, flex time off, tuition remission, a 403(b) \nwith employer match, employee wellness time, and more. \n \nReady to Apply? \nWe can't wait to hear from you!  During the application process, please be prepared to upload a letter of \napplication, current curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and current contact information \nfor three professional references. \n \nPlease apply using the following link: Physician Assistant Studies Faculty "
    }
  },
